# Triango ARM32 Bridge — SELinux additions (Magisk/KernelSU sepolicy.rule).
#
# ksud applies these on boot / late-load. Keep this list minimal; Triango is
# designed to work under enforcing. Rules that fail to load (unknown types on
# a given build) are ignored by the policy tool.
#
# 1) The setup scripts mount binfmt_misc and register a handler.
allow { magisk kernel } tmpfs filesystem { mount getattr }
# 2) Executing the AArch64 bridge and its engine from /data/adb/triango.
allow { magisk kernel } adb_data_file dir { search read open getattr }
allow { magisk kernel } adb_data_file file { read open execute getattr map }
